.SS noust create
Deploy a web application and put it online.
.TP
.B \-d, \-\-domain
Domain the application is served on.
.TP
.B \-s, \-\-source
Git URL, archive URL or directory to deploy from. Not with \-\-recipe.
.TP
.B \-\-recipe
Deploy a known application from its recipe (see 'noust recipe list'): its source, type, database and settings come from the recipe.
.TP
.B \-\-env
Set a variable of the application environment, over \-\-env\-file and a recipe's own. Repeat for several.
.TP
.B \-t, \-\-type
Application type. Detected from the source when left on auto. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-p, \-\-port
Port the application listens on. A free one is chosen when omitted.
.TP
.B \-w, \-\-webserver
Web server that fronts the application. Default: nginx.
.TP
.B \-b, \-\-branch
Git branch to deploy.
.TP
.B \-\-follow\-tags
Deploy the newest git tag that matches this glob (such as 'v*') and keep deploying new ones, from a release or a tag push, instead of following a branch.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-ssl
Serve over plain HTTP, without a certificate.
.TP
.B \-\-www
Also answer on www.<domain>, redirecting it to the domain (see 'noust domain').
.TP
.B \-\-env\-file
File of KEY=value lines to install as the application environment.
.TP
.B \-\-package\-manager, \-\-pm
Node package manager. Detected from the lockfile when left on auto. Default: auto.
.TP
.B \-\-subdomains
Serve a monorepo app on this subdomain. Repeat once per app.
.TP
.B \-\-workspaces
Deploy only this monorepo workspace. Repeat to select several.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-database
Skip database provisioning for a monorepo.
.TP
.B \-\-database
Create a database for the application before its first build, owned by an account of its own, with its connection string in the environment (DATABASE_URL, REDIS_URL for Redis). NAME defaults to one derived from the domain. Not with \-\-recipe.
.TP
.B \-\-database\-version
The version of the \-\-database engine, such as 17 or 11.4. The installed one when omitted; one the server does not run is refused with what it runs.
.TP
.B \-\-install\-database
Install the \-\-database engine, in \-\-database\-version, when it is not installed. Installs packages: the same as 'noust db install'.
.TP
.B \-\-database\-instance
Make the \-\-database on this instance Noust runs ('noust db instance list') instead of the host's engine. One is also chosen by itself when \-\-database\-version is what an instance runs and the host does not.
.TP
.B \-\-compose\-file
Compose file to use, relative to the project. Detected when omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-compose\-profiles
Activate this Docker Compose profile. Repeat to activate several.
.TP
.B \-\-layout
Build every deploy as a release behind a health gate, or in place. Defaults to the server's deploy.layout.
.TP
.B \-\-persist
Keep this path, relative to the app, in shared/ across releases. Repeat for several.
.TP
.B \-\-build\-file
A YAML file holding 'build:' (base_directory, install, build, start, publish_directory, runtime): the operator's block for this application, which replaces the repository's noust.yaml and is kept for every update. How several applications are deployed from one repository: see docs/build.md.
.TP
.B \-\-force
Deploy into an app directory that already holds files: in place a git checkout is brought up to date, keeping what git does not track (.env, data), and anything else is refused, never emptied; on releases a release is added beside them.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-cache
Build the first deployment without any cache: images without their layer cache.
.TP
.B \-\-registry
A registry account (noust registry add) to pull private images with, for a Docker Compose or container application. Repeat it for several.
.TP
.B \-\-image
Deploy this image from a registry: name[:tag][@sha256:digest]. Needs no source.
.TP
.B \-\-builder
How a repository becomes an image: its Dockerfile, or Railpack, which needs none (noust setup railpack).
.TP
.B \-\-dockerfile
The Dockerfile, relative to the repository. Default: Dockerfile or Containerfile in the context.
.TP
.B \-\-context
The build context, relative to the repository. Default: its root.
.TP
.B \-\-target
The stage of a multi\-stage Dockerfile to build.
.TP
.B \-\-build\-arg
A build argument (not a secret: it is written into the image). Repeat for several.
.TP
.B \-\-build\-secret
A secret the build mounts, read from FILE and kept in the secret store; never an argument of the build. Repeat for several.
.TP
.B \-\-container\-port
Where the process listens inside the container. Default: what the Dockerfile or the image exposes.
.TP
.B \-\-volume
A path in the container whose data survives every deployment, such as /data. Repeat for several.
.TP
.B \-\-restart
Docker's restart policy: no, always, unless\-stopped (default) or on\-failure.
.TP
.B \-\-registry\-server
The registry the account is for. Default: the image's own.
.TP
.B \-\-registry\-user
The account of a private registry.
.TP
.B \-\-registry\-password\-stdin
Read the account's password from standard input.
.TP
.B \-\-team
The team it belongs to (default: the default team).
.TP
.B \-\-project
The project it belongs to (default: the team's default).
.TP
.B \-\-environment
The environment it belongs to (default: production).
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show the detail of each step.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Rehearse without changing anything. Read\-only checks still run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Never emit colour.
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

