Give an application a database's connection string, and restart it.
.TP
.B Arguments
.br
\fIdomain\fR
.br
\fIdatabase\fR
.TP
.B \-\-engine, \-e
Engine the database is on.
.TP
.B \-\-user, \-u
Account to sign in as. Noust must know it.
.TP
.B \-\-env\-var
Variable to write. DATABASE_URL, or REDIS_URL for Redis.
.TP
.B \-\-extra\-vars
Also write DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_NAME, ...
.TP
.B \-\-tls
Make the application encrypt the connection and, with verify\-ca or verify\-full, check the engine's certificate against Noust's authority. Needs an engine that serves TLS (noust db instance tls).
.TP
.B \-\-no\-restart
Write the variables without restarting.
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

