Create a database and an account for an application, and link them.
.TP
.B Arguments
.br
\fIdomain\fR
.TP
.B \-\-engine, \-e
Engine to create it on.
.TP
.B \-\-name
Database name. Derived from the application by default.
.TP
.B \-\-env\-var
Variable to write. DATABASE_URL, or REDIS_URL for Redis.
.TP
.B \-\-extra\-vars
Also write DB_HOST, DB_PORT, DB_NAME, ...
.TP
.B \-\-no\-restart
Write the variables without restarting.
.TP
.B \-\-version
The version of the engine the database is for, such as 17 or 11.4 ('noust db choices' lists them). The installed one when omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-install
Install the engine, in \-\-version, first when it is not installed: the same as 'noust db install'.
.TP
.B \-\-instance
Make it on this instance Noust runs ('noust db instance list') instead of the host's engine. One is also chosen by itself when \-\-version is what an instance runs and the host does not.
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

