.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

.SS noust db public open
Make DATABASE reachable from the network: a public port, an account of its own, the firewall.
.TP
.B Arguments
.br
\fIdatabase\fR
.TP
.B \-\-engine, \-e
Engine the database is on.
.TP
.B \-\-port
The public port. A free one near the engine's is chosen.
.TP
.B \-\-bind
Address to listen on: 0.0.0.0 (every IPv4 address, the default), :: or one address.
.TP
.B \-\-from
Let only this address or network (CIDR) in; repeat for several. Anyone when omitted.
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-plaintext
Do not require TLS. The password and the data then cross the network in clear.
.TP
.B \-\-access
What the account made for it may do on this database. Default: owner.
.TP
.B \-\-yes, \-y
Accept every warning without asking.
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show the detail of each step.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Rehearse without changing anything. Read\-only checks still run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Never emit colour.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the outcome (with the password, once) as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

