.SS noust preview enable
Turn previews on for an application, or change their settings.
.TP
.B Arguments
.br
\fIdomain\fR
.TP
.B \-\-domain
Base domain previews answer under; *.BASE must point at this server. Required to turn previews on; kept when changing other settings.
.TP
.B \-\-max
How many previews may exist at once (1 to 20). [default: 3, or the current value]
.TP
.B \-\-ttl
How long a preview lives without a push: 12h, 7d, 2w (1 hour to 90 days). [default: 7d, or the current value]
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-bots, \-\-no\-allow\-bots
Build previews of pull requests opened or pushed to by bot accounts (Dependabot, Renovate). [default: no, or the current value]
.TP
.B \-\-exclude\-env
A variable never copied to previews; repeat for more. Replaces the current list; existing previews lose them at their next push.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-exclude\-env
Copy every variable again (clear the excluded list).
.TP
.B \-\-env\-mode
Which of the application's variables a preview is given: 'allowlist' (only \-\-allow\-env, the default for previews turned on now) or 'all' (every one less \-\-exclude\-env, as before 3.4).
.TP
.B \-\-allow\-env
A variable an 'allowlist' preview copies; repeat for more. Replaces the current list.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-allow\-env
Copy no variable of the application's (clear the allowed list).
.TP
.B \-\-data
'empty' gives each preview a database of its own, 'clone' a database of its own that starts as a copy of the application's, 'shared' lets it use the application's (a pull request can then write into production's). Default for previews turned on now: empty, when the application has a database.
.TP
.B \-\-domain\-template
How a preview is named, such as '{{pr_id}}\-{{name}}.{{base}}' ({{pr_id}}, {{random}}, {{domain}}, {{name}}, {{base}}); '' goes back to pr\-<n>\-<name>.BASE. Applies to the previews made from now on.
.TP
.B \-\-noindex, \-\-index
Tell search engines to leave previews alone (X\-Robots\-Tag). [default: noindex]
.TP
.B \-\-forks
'refuse' (a pull request from a fork, or from someone not trusted with the repository, gets no preview) or 'approve' (it waits for an operator to approve each commit: noust preview approve). [default: refuse]
.TP
.B \-v, \-\-verbose
Show the detail of each step.
.TP
.B \-\-dry\-run
Rehearse without changing anything. Read\-only checks still run.
.TP
.B \-\-no\-color
Never emit colour.
.TP
.B \-\-json
Print the settings as JSON.
.TP
.B \-\-reason
Why this change is made (a change reference, a ticket). Recorded with the command in the audit log; required by the ens\-medium security profile.

